        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="CAR06" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John Aitken</forename>
                        <surname>Carlyle</surname>
                        <addName>Jack</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1801-07-07">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1879-09-15"/>
                    <occupation>physician</occupation>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>John was the brother of <persName key="CAR03">Thomas Carlyle</persName>. He graduated MD from the University of Edinburgh in 1826. He later tried to earn a living 
    from writing in London. He attended <persName key="HAZ01">William Hazlitt</persName> when Hazlitt was dying. He spent a number of years working as a travelling physician to 
    the aristocracy, a period which included a seven year stint in Italy. He married well and devoted himself to literary pursuits in later life.</p>
                        <p>Godwin's one entry is to meeting the Carlyles (noting that they were from Edinburgh) in 1831. For a full account of the visit, from Thomas Carlyle's point of view, see his entry. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
